      "heading": "ECET:",
      "heading_level": 1,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text": "ECET:\nCOMPUTER SCIENCE & ENGINEERING - M.Tech\nDepartment Vision and Mission\nTo be in the frontiers of Computer Science and Engineering with academic excellence and Research.\nEducate students with the best practices of Computer Science by integrating the latest research into the curriculum.\nDevelop professionals with sound knowledge in theory and practice of Computer Science and Engineering.\nFacilitate the development of academia-industry collaboration and societal outreach programs.\nPrepare students for full and ethical participation in a diverse society and encourage lifelong learning.\nHOD of CSE & IT",
      "token_count": 97
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "MTech-cse-info.php.json_chunk_1",
      "chunk_index": 1,
      "heading": "Dr. Nagavelli Ramana",
      "heading_level": 2,
      "chunk_type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Dr. Nagavelli Ramana\nPrincipal, HOD of CSE, IT, CSD\n9885288905\nramanauce.ku@gmail.com\nDepartment of Computer Science & Engineering\nThe\nDepartment of Computer Science and Engineering (CSE)\nprogram focuses on the study of computer systems, software development, algorithms, and data processing.\nIt provides students with a strong foundation in Programming, Data-Structures and Algorithms, Computer Architecture, Networking, Artificial Intelligence, and Machine learning.\nThe curriculum combines theoretical knowledge with hands-on projects and lab sessions, preparing students to solve complex computational problems.\nGraduates are equipped with technical skills relevant to careers in\nsoftware development\n,\ndata science\n,\ncybersecurity\n, and\nresearch\n, and are well-prepared for both industry roles and further studies in computer science.\nThe curriculum combines theoretical knowledge with hands-on projects and lab sessions, preparing students to solve complex computational problems. Graduates are equipped with technical skills relevant to careers in\nsoftware development\n,\ndata science\n,\ncybersecurity\n, and\nresearch\n, and are well-prepared for both industry roles and further studies in computer science.",
      "token_count": 201
    },
